      "amendment_rationale": "2026-08-04 peer-review round 2. The abstract was rewritten on the supervisor's dictated shape and no longer quotes the M0 first-contact aggregate, so an entry anchored on 'Here we show that a physics-grounded wall closure' and requiring M0 tokens could never pass. The entry is retargeted, not weakened: it now binds the two quantitative claims the abstract actually makes -- the cube wall-force error falling by two-fifths (0.09944 -> 0.06093) and the channel closure recovering three-quarters of the record's own traction benefit (0.11984 / 0.16497 = 0.726) -- each to its own source file, and additionally requires the abstract to state that the separating hill transmits in only one of the two generative families, so the adverse preregistered arm cannot be dropped from the abstract without failing this check. The retired M0 refs remain verified by the first_contact_m0 entries elsewhere in this contract.  2026-08-05 supervisor revision. The abstract was rewritten again on the supervisor's instruction (superlative softened, the equilibrium lift named as the commonly adopted fix, long sentences split, and the three records named with the rationale for choosing two hard ones). That rewrite removed the phrase 'Supplied instead as conditioning' on which this entry was anchored, so the entry matched an empty region and every token read false. The anchor is retargeted to 'the surface quantity propagates', which audit_level1_protocol independently requires the abstract to contain and which therefore cannot silently disappear. The three required tokens are unchanged in substance; the hill token is now stored without the embedded line break that tied it to one particular text wrapping. No guarantee is weakened: the abstract must still disclose both quantitative claims and the adverse one-of-two-families result.  2026-08-10 supervisor meeting revision. The abstract was expanded to the dictated opening (generative models gaining attention with the hope of a step change; a full stop after 'engineering loads'; a dedicated volume-averaged-objective sentence; 'commonly used' replacing 'obvious'; a closing refocus statement) and then trimmed back under the journal's 200-word ceiling. The trim shortened the propagation clause to 'the stress propagates', so the anchor is retargeted to that phrase, which audit_level1_protocol now independently requires. The three required tokens and all four source bindings are unchanged; no guarantee is weakened."
